package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"strings"
)

const (
	shellModule = "Theorems.RationalLocalPairedShellTrial"
	shellDecl   = "Masullo.rationalLocalPairedShell_trial"
	unitModule  = "Theorems.PadicTranslatedUnitLogTrial"
	unitDecl    = "Masullo.padicTranslatedUnitLog_trial"
)

func prompt(a arm, seed string) string {
	schedule := "Dispatch writer-a; wait for its successful terminal notification before attempting writer-b."
	if a == concurrent {
		schedule = "Dispatch writer-a and then immediately writer-b, before requesting any join or doing other work. A launch acknowledgment is not a terminal notification. If there is no actual overlap, report that the treatment failed."
	}
	return fmt.Sprintf(`You own one disposable proofpair campaign. Do not read or seek other arms or upstream history. Do not run cmd/godel except the existing audit-local entry point, run remote check, start services, use network/retrieval/publication tools, or push anything. Do not change the control checkout. Stop on any failed gate; record incomplete evidence rather than repair or retry. Use no other agent tools beyond the three fresh direct dispatches below. Never resume or fork.

Before dispatch, require tool_campaign(op=status, verbose=true): available=true, accepted=%s, attempt_count=0, output_count=0, and no tracked_target or target_divergence. The launcher selects local main; tracked_target denotes a divergent remote commit, not the local bookmark name. Local main may move only at final adoption. Every writer's tool_subagent revision is the FULL synthetic seed %s (even writer-b in the sequential arm). Each timeout_seconds is 1800. Pass the corresponding writer brief below in message without adding schedule, prior results, or arm identity. Set intent for each writer to "Fresh nonrecursive Lean proof writer; select %s at %s effort; preserve the task message and use the fixed workspace revision." No other selector fields are supported.

%s
Use tool_yield alone while waiting on pending work. Use no steering or result transfers between writers. Do not yield with nothing pending.
Wait for terminal notifications and campaign status confirming both successful, distinct, nonconflicted registered outputs at the seed. Check dispatch evidence in $HOME/.yah/sessions/<this-uuid>/agents/ before using results: each chosen model %s, effective effort %s, nonrecursive, expected timeout/base and task message. Check early when possible (without inserting work between concurrent launches); stop on mismatch. A failed launch, timeout, missing terminal or output, or out-of-scope change ends the arm. Do not launch unused work after detecting failure. Compare outputs to the seed: exactly one added regular Lean file per writer as specified, no other edits.

Writer A brief:
%s

Writer B brief:
%s

Only you integrate: exactly one tool_campaign integrate with on=%s, outputs=[registered A commit, registered B commit], description="Combine rational local proof trial endpoints". Keep its exact candidate ID and workspace. Confirm no conflicts and precisely the union of the two added files, with their exact bytes. No hand merge or candidate repair. After integration dispatch exactly one fresh read-only statement review, slug statement-review, revision=exact candidate, timeout_seconds=900. Intent: "Fresh nonrecursive Lean mathematical statement reviewer; select %s at %s effort; preserve the task message." Use this exact review brief:
%s

Require a terminal OK and explicit pass on both statements with no tracked edits; check review dispatch model/effort/base/nonrecursion/scope. Then in the integration workspace (not a writer/review workspace), copy the read-only baseline build into its private .lake/build if absent (cp --archive --reflink=auto /srv/proofpair/base/.lake/build <integration workspace>/.lake/build). Do not copy any writer/reviewer build. Run once (quote the workspace path):
  cd <returned integration workspace> && /opt/proofpair/bin/godel-base audit-local <full candidate ID> %s %s -- %s %s >"$HOME/proofpair-audit.log" 2>&1
Require exit zero and log line "Local build and kernel/axiom audit passed for <full candidate ID> (%s, %s)." Verify the invocation used both declaration arguments; the success line itself names only the commit and modules. Retain the redirected log, including on failure. That binary is the unchanged base cmd/godel built for its audit-local entry point. Only then tool_campaign(op=adopt, candidate=<full candidate ID>), once, locally to main, and require accepted=candidate, stale=false. Do not navigate to newer revisions or publish. Keep full diagnostics in the session. In your final response report stage, writer terminals and commits, candidate/attempt, review verdicts, audit modules/declarations/status, adoption result and any deviations. Exit text alone is not evidence.`, seed, seed, model, effort, schedule, model, effort, writerA, writerB, seed, review, effort, reviewBrief, shellModule, unitModule, shellDecl, unitDecl, shellModule, unitModule)
}

var writerA = strings.TrimSpace(fmt.Sprintf(`Prove the runnable paired rational finite Haar shells obligation at this frozen base. Read .godel/obligations/rational-explicit-formula.md ("Next runnable obligation: Evaluate the rational finite Haar shells") and the pinned manuscript via GRH_PDF (pp. 622–623, 625). For rational finite v with corresponding prime p, every m>=1, and continuous compactly supported real F, work in the units of the actual rational local completion, not a stand-in field. The two shells norm x=p^(-m),p^m are translates of the integral unit range by uniformizer powers, each of unit mass for rationalLocalMultiplicativeHaar. Show norm(1-x)=1 and norm(1-x)=norm x on the respective shells. Use the genuine normalized subtracted radial integrand: off the integral unit group it is (log p) * (sqrt(norm x) * F(log(norm x))) / norm(1-x); on the integral unit group it is zero. The endpoint equates the sum of the two restricted integrals to (log p) * p^(-m/2) * (F(-m log p)+F(m log p)), with real powers or equivalent expressions. Prove the shell facts and that only finitely many paired terms can be nonzero at fixed p; tie the samples to the existing compactLogMellin_prime_power_evaluation at n=p^m for g(t)=exp(-t/2)F(t); no global comparison. Do not assume the desired integral or shell identities. Add only Proofs/%s.lean and expose %s as the public integral endpoint. Helpers must live in that file. Use only the base inputs and your fresh workspace; do not inspect other workspaces, journals, or results. No revision management, sorry, new axioms, or bypasses. Validate using a literal lake build command (to seed the private build from the baseline cache), then report the exact endpoint and status.`, strings.ReplaceAll(shellModule, ".", "/"), shellDecl))

var writerB = strings.TrimSpace(fmt.Sprintf(`Prove the runnable translated rational unit indicator calibration obligation at this frozen base. Read .godel/obligations/rational-explicit-formula.md ("Upstream calibration test: The translated rational unit indicator") and the pinned manuscript via GRH_PDF (pp. 621–623). For every prime p, on Q_p with padicAddHaar p of mass 1 on B=Z_p, take u=1_B-1_{-1+pB}, the translated unit-indicator test (zero at -1). Use the negative standard-character kernel in padicTranslatedBall_fourier. The endpoint asserts integrability AND vanishing of the complex pairing of (log(norm ξ)/log p) with the actual additive Fourier transform of u. Use the two ball transforms (or a proved equivalent); do not assume the shell integral, cancellation, or Fourier identity. Do not assert a general local comparison. Add only Proofs/%s.lean and expose %s as the public integrability-and-vanishing endpoint. Helpers must live in that file. Use only the base inputs and your fresh workspace; do not inspect other workspaces, journals, or results. No revision management, sorry, new axioms, or bypasses. Validate using a literal lake build command (to seed the private build from the baseline cache), then report the exact endpoint and status.`, strings.ReplaceAll(unitModule, ".", "/"), unitDecl))

var reviewBrief = fmt.Sprintf(`Read-only statement review of one combined candidate. Do not edit tracked files or inspect other workspaces, journals, or upstream history. First build both modules with a literal lake build command (to seed the private build from the baseline cache). Compare each exact elaborated public statement and the definitions it relies on (inspect #check with lake env lean --stdin) to its frozen obligation and pinned manuscript (GRH_PDF). A: %s in %s must integrate the correct unit-subtracted radial profile on both actual rational-completion shells with unit-mass Haar, prime/time/half-powers and Mellin substitutions as in the handoff. Check that named helpers establish the shell facts, finite support at fixed p, and Mellin sample identities rather than assuming them. B: %s in %s must assert both integrability and exact zero for the log ratio paired with the negative-kernel transform of the translated unit test in Q_p, with correct normalized Haar, not a pairing against its original support. Check for weakened quantifiers, vacuous hypotheses, altered definitions, trivialized tests or identities, and accidental extra scope. Return a separate explicit PASS or FAIL with reason and elaborated type evidence for each. This is not the kernel/axiom audit.`, shellDecl, shellModule, unitDecl, unitModule)
